==Evolution==
Evolves into '''Blizana''' at level 10.

Evolves into '''Blizarena''' at level 30 using [[Catfruit]] and XP.

==Strategy/Usage==
Bliza's main point of interest is how their multi-hit's range expands with each hit. This would theoretically increase its crowd-controlling capabilities because at least one other hit will land if Bliza lands the first one, but that's not the case. Its ability only occurs on the final hit, meaning that its slow will not proc if missed. Luckily, Bliza's Omni-Strike expands to about 550 range ahead, so missing the final hit shouldn't be seen often. Unfortunately, its low range drags this down a lot, so Bliza needs stepping stones to be able to snipe and crowd control backliners properly. Bliza's immunity to Slow is also quite situational, as it only helps them to counter [[Galactic Overseer Nyandam]], [[Queen B]] and [[Super Hyppoh]]. Additionally, it can be helpful with their tanking abilities in its Zombie niche for the waves of them appearing in [[Parade of the Dead (Deadly)|Parade of the Dead]] and [[Prisoner's Progress (Merciless)|Prisoner's Progress]] especially.

Blizana's evolved or true forms perform very well in zombie outbreaks, in both [[Into the Future]] and [[Cats of the Cosmos]]. Targeting aliens and zombies with resistance and slow is very useful, and she also has zombie killer and barrier breaker to sweeten the deal. Omnistrike can pick up zombies standing right behind her as well.

Bliza was designed to fight against [[Super Hyppoh]] and [[Big Peng Z]], but even then it struggles against these enemies due to having low range. Especially against [[Big Peng Z]], it struggles due to the lack of toxic immunity. As an anti-Zombie specialist, Omni Strike can be useful, but there would be no point in slowing as by the time Bliza finishes the final hit the Zombies may have already burrowed. Also remember to not rely on this unit as your only source of damage, as Bliza has a sluggish attack rate and low DPS. However, it can still work as a good sniper as they can break barriers from 550 range away, but don't expect it to perform well as a generalist.

==='''True Form'''===
The main buffs for Blizarena are a 50% HP increase and a considerably slighter 4.1667% attack increase. While the latter is negligible, the former alone allows Blizana to tank enemies far more effectively and use her CC far more effectively.

On that note, an extra second of backswing and an extra second of Slow allow it to keep enemies controlled for longer while increasing their own longevity.

Blizarena also gains Toxic Immunity to dismiss a wide variety of such threats in mixed stages, such as [[Requiem for Angels (Merciless)|Requiem for Angels]] ([[Heavenly Herald Papuu]] and [[UltraBaaBaa]]), as well as becoming usable for [[Big Peng Z]]. The health boost allows it to tank the other Zombies in [[Big Peng Z Strikes/Wandering Lv.1~20|Wandering levels 11 and beyond]] comfortably, and the slow duration increase is likewise helpful to inhibit enemy pushers.

==='''Talents'''===
'''[[Slow]]''' increases the ability's duration by a meager 1 second, bringing it up to 6 seconds, or a 75% uptime with [[Fruit Treasures]]. Since this ability is her main selling point, improving it isn't a bad investment, but it's generally not worth the 175 NP.

[[Special Abilities#Resist|Resist Freeze]] is basically worthless, and only helps slightly in niche situations against [[Deathshund]], [[Zir Zeal]], [[Henry]], [[Maawth]], and [[Death Angel Z-Onel]]. However, she functions perfectly fine without it.

'''Cost Down''' is exactly what it appears on paper. It's not exactly a bang for your buck, and the cost difference between 3,630 and 3,180 is hardly noticeable. Still a straightforward improvement, though, just not worth its weight in NP.

'''Attack Buff''' and '''HP Buff''' should not be considered until you have upgraded Blizarena with [[Catseye]]s. Generally, HP Buff helps her more considering her somewhat low range; longevity is king.

